{"availability":"available","full":"eliemichel/SlangWebGPU","name":"SlangWebGPU","description":"A possible use of Slang shader compiler together with WebGPU in C++ (both in native and Web contexts), using CMake.","category":"Design","language":"C++","stars":83,"forks":2,"created":"2024-11-23T08:39:05Z","updated":"2024-11-29T00:05:51Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://shader-slang.com/slang-playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:01:17.392Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:01:17.392Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:01:17.392Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:19.999Z","stars":83,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-10T13:01:33.966Z","stars":83,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.073Z","stars":83,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-19T18:01:17.392Z","stars":83,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["LearnWebGPU | WebGPU-C++ | WebGPU-distribution","Slang is a great modern shader programming language, but of course it does not natively run in WebGPU. One possible workaround is to ship the Slang compiler to the client, but this is heavy both in bandwidth and client computation time, so this setup rather transpiles shaders into WGSL (WebGPU shading language) at compilation time.","Compiling shaders are one thing, but when working on a shader-intensive application, one easily spends too much time writing kernel binding boilerplate rather than actuall business logic (i.e., the nice things we actually want to code). Among Slang's nice features is a reflection API, which this project benefits from to automatically generate kernel binding code."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eliemichel/SlangWebGPU/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"58d67ac4e10d8b71cfa76d20a8fa621bd71b174a68b57ebb7d96276a347b54cb","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:20.140Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.187Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"LearnWebGPU | WebGPU-C++ | WebGPU-distribution","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eliemichel/SlangWebGPU/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"58d67ac4e10d8b71cfa76d20a8fa621bd71b174a68b57ebb7d96276a347b54cb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eliemichel/SlangWebGPU/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.187Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-11-29T00:05:51Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eliemichel/SlangWebGPU/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.188Z","hash":"58d67ac4e10d8b71cfa76d20a8fa621bd71b174a68b57ebb7d96276a347b54cb","originalBytes":14586,"storedBytes":14586,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:41.073Z","subjects":["3D & graphics"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Design","subjects":["3D & graphics"],"evidence":[{"subject":"3D & graphics","source":"metadata","match":"shader"}],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Automation & workflows","Templates & UI components"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://shader-slang.com/slang-playground/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-15T05:12:08.210Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T05:12:08.210Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-15T05:12:08.210Z","target":"https://shader-slang.org/slang-playground/","failureCount":0,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-22T05:12:08.210Z"},"previewAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T05:12:08.210Z","previewCheck":{"url":"https://shader-slang.com/slang-playground/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-15T05:12:08.210Z","consecutiveFailures":0,"status":"captured","reason":null,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-22T05:12:08.210Z"},"screenshots":[{"src":"previews/cb162c754cb36b8e1320678a.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2026-10-15T05:12:08.210Z","url":"https://shader-slang.com/slang-playground/"}],"qualityPriority":false,"repositoryEtag":"W/\"650f6398285a7046c35dc31aea269c701e1d74978b5fe297d0